g laparoscopic cholecystectomy: technical considerations</article-title><source>Surg Endosc</source><year>2006</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1654</fpage><lpage>1658</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00464-006-0488-3</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Callery MP (2006) Avoiding biliary injury during laparoscopic cholecystectomy: technical considerations. Surg Endosc 20:1654&#x02013;1658 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17063288</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="other">Kuwada T (2005) Highlights of The Society of American Gastrointestinal and Endoscopic Surgeons 2005 Annual Meeting, April 2005, Ft. Lauderdale, FL. Medscape General Surgery, May (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.medscape.com/generalsurgery">http://www.medscape.com/generalsurgery</ext-link>)</citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Strasberg</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hertl</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Soper</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An analysis of the problem of biliary injury during laparoscopic cholecystectomy</article-title><source>J Am Coll Surg</source><year>1995</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>125</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Strasberg SM, Hertl M, Soper NJ (1995) An analysis of the problem of biliary injury during laparoscopic cholecystectomy. J Am Coll Surg 180:101&#x02013;125 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8000648</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Way</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gantert</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Causes and prevention of laparoscopic bile duct injuries: analysis of 252 cases from a human factors and cognitive psychology perspective</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>2003</year><volume>237</volume><fpage>460</fpage><lpage>469</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000658-200304000-00004</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Way LW, Stewart L, Gantert W, et&#x000a0;al (2003) Causes and prevention of laparoscopic bile duct injuries: analysis of 252 cases from a human factors and cognitive psychology perspective. Ann Surg 237:460&#x02013;469 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12677139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Plaisier</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Pauwels</surname><given-names>MMA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lange</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality control in laparoscopic cholecystectomy: operation notes, video or photo print?</article-title><source>HPB Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>199</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Plaisier PW, Pauwels MMA, Lange JF (2001) Quality control in laparoscopic cholecystectomy: operation notes, video or photo print? HPB Surg 3:197&#x02013;199 </citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kohn</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name><name><surname>Corrigan</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Donaldson</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><source>To err is human: building a safer health system</source><year>2000</year><publisher-loc>Washington DC</publisher-loc><publisher-name>National Academy Press</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kohn LT, Corrigan JM, Donaldson MS (2000) To err is human: building a safer health system. National Academy Press, Washington DC </citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Degani</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiener</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cockpit checklists: concepts, design and use human factors</article-title><source>Hum Factors</source><year>1993</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>345</fpage><lpage>359</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Degani A, Wiener EL (1993) Cockpit checklists: concepts, design and use human factors. Hum Factors 35:345&#x02013;359 </citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Undre</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sevdalis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Healey</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Teamwork in the operating theatre: cohesion or confusion?</article-title><source>J Eval Clin Pract</source><year>2006</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>182</fpage><lpage>189</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2753.2006.00614.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Undre S, Sevdalis N, Healey AN, et&#x000a0;al (2006) Teamwork in the operating theatre: cohesion or confusion? J Eval Clin Pract 12:182&#x02013;189 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16579827</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Healey</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name><name><surname>Undre</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><artic